content.text:
Now restructure updatePools to not stack. Also add a subtle indicator if multiple pools. I'll rewrite the function.

Current updatePools loops each pool and each unit. New:

```js
updatePools(dt) {
  for (let i = this.pools.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    const pool = this.pools[i];
    pool.life -= dt;
    if (pool.life <= 0) this.pools.splice(i, 1);
  }
  for (const u of this.units) {
    if (!u.alive) continue;
    let lava = null;
    for (const pool of this.pools) {
      if (pool.team === u.team) continue;
      const nx = (u.x - pool.x) / pool.r;
      const ny = (u.y - pool.y) / (pool.r * 0.62);
      if (nx*nx + ny*ny < 1 && (!lava || pool.dps > lava.dps)) lava = pool;
    }
    if (!lava) continue;
    u.slowT = 0.1;
    this.damage(u, lava.dps * dt, lava.owner, { silent: true, burn: true });
    u.poolAcc = (u.poolAcc || 0) + lava.dps * dt;
    if (u.poolAcc > 14) { u.poolAcc = 0; this.spawnFloat(...); }
    if (Math.random() < dt * 8) { spawn particle using u }
  }
}
```

Wait `damage` might kill u; after damage, if dead, don't spawn particle? Current code checks math random after damage; if killed then still does particles and the loop continues; but kill sets alive=false, next unit check. It's okay but guard.

Also, there's a subtle issue: if player stands in 2 pools of same dps, only one. Great.

Additionally, overlapping friendly pools visually combine. Good.

Apply.

